# Wave W17-R (Route 124 Trench): shaft wall — shaft rock: a blue-grey trench rock laid in jointed courses, pale rim flecks standing on its upper faces where the light shafts strike the walls on their way down (design: the road under the road, its walls catching the same light as its floor). Route 124 Trench’s own wall — blue-grey and jointed where Route 126 Trench’s door wall is dark warm crater rock in arch courses: the lit crossing’s wall against the drowned doorway’s.
